Hey Believe Nation, thank
you so much for watching.

00:05:41.862 --> 00:05:43.893
If you want to learn
more about this subject,

00:05:43.893 --> 00:05:46.270
get a little bit deeper
on it, I'm going to share

00:05:46.270 --> 00:05:48.895
some extra bonus clips
that I hope you'll enjoy.

00:05:48.895 --> 00:05:52.478
- When I was younger,
about 16, 17, 18, 19,

00:05:54.201 --> 00:05:57.701
I was more creating worlds and characters.

00:05:58.581 --> 00:06:03.113
I would read a lot just
because me liking to learn,

00:06:03.113 --> 00:06:06.780
I would read about
certain people and try to

00:06:07.955 --> 00:06:12.157
get in their head and see
how they would write a song.

00:06:12.157 --> 00:06:15.772
Now I kind of just write about my life.

00:06:15.772 --> 00:06:18.318
I have this song called
hair blows on the new album

00:06:18.318 --> 00:06:20.981
that's just talking about I
like when this girl's hair blows

00:06:20.981 --> 00:06:24.614
in the car, and I wrote
that because I was with

00:06:24.614 --> 00:06:27.674
a female friend of
mine, we were in my car,

00:06:27.674 --> 00:06:30.388
and she was hanging out the
sunroof and her hair was blowing

00:06:30.388 --> 00:06:33.739
and felt like the man, and
I wrote a song about it.

00:06:33.739 --> 00:06:37.906
I think a lot of artists
mess up because you don't

00:06:39.772 --> 00:06:43.412
know much about them after
a certain point in time.

00:06:43.412 --> 00:06:46.991
I realized none of my
music would sound the same

00:06:46.991 --> 00:06:50.837
if I just wrote songs
actually about my life.

00:06:50.837 --> 00:06:53.994
Every two years you should
not be in the same place.

00:06:53.994 --> 00:06:56.363
- But it does take some courage though to

00:06:56.363 --> 00:06:57.671
be so transparent about your own life.

00:06:57.671 --> 00:06:59.216
- A lot of people aren't honest because

00:06:59.216 --> 00:07:00.991
they're not comfortable with themselves

00:07:00.991 --> 00:07:01.990
- [Interviewer] That's right.

00:07:01.990 --> 00:07:03.518
- So that's why you have
a bunch of songs about

00:07:03.518 --> 00:07:05.797
the same things on the
radio because one, it's

00:07:05.797 --> 00:07:08.640
comforting to a simple
listener, and two, people

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:11.676
just aren't comfortable with themselves.

00:07:11.676 --> 00:07:14.489
If I was like hey, I'm depressed.

00:07:14.489 --> 00:07:16.288
You'd be like "wow,"
'cause a lot of people

00:07:16.288 --> 00:07:18.083
won't be able to do that
or tell you what they like

00:07:18.083 --> 00:07:20.813
and stand for it and why they like it.

00:07:20.813 --> 00:07:24.902
That goes again with a lot
of people being close-minded.

00:07:24.902 --> 00:07:27.781
- Here's the thing though
people see you on stage,

00:07:27.781 --> 00:07:30.479
they see you on tour for
years, we know you do well.

00:07:30.479 --> 00:07:34.146
It's documented, but I
try to get onlookers,

00:07:35.204 --> 00:07:38.787
fans, listeners, to
understand that there's

00:07:40.276 --> 00:07:43.786
no difference necessarily in people.

00:07:43.786 --> 00:07:46.007
- We all have the same emotions.

00:07:46.007 --> 00:07:48.666
- Same emotions, we all go
through the same issues.

00:07:48.666 --> 00:07:50.851
And even though you see
Tech N9ne on this show

00:07:50.851 --> 00:07:54.474
in the morning or you might see
him on some award show stage

00:07:54.474 --> 00:07:57.797
behind closed doors, he's experienced

00:07:57.797 --> 00:08:00.285
the same thing your neighbor
might be experiencing.

00:08:00.285 --> 00:08:02.995
- And that's how we make fans.

00:08:02.995 --> 00:08:06.578
It brings us down to
a level playing field,

00:08:07.555 --> 00:08:10.972
'cause they look at us elevated on stage.

00:08:11.999 --> 00:08:14.414
They automatically looking
up, so when you tell them

00:08:14.414 --> 00:08:17.463
I'm having a bad day because
my people are turning on me

00:08:17.463 --> 00:08:19.374
and I thought these people were real.

00:08:19.374 --> 00:08:21.531
It brings us on a level playing field.

00:08:21.531 --> 00:08:24.173
He feels just like me,
that's how we make fans.

00:08:24.173 --> 00:08:28.035
I tapped into emotions
and a lot of my fans

00:08:28.035 --> 00:08:30.536
know about my life because
I put it in my records.

00:08:30.536 --> 00:08:34.683
My wife didn't like,
when This Ring came out,

00:08:34.683 --> 00:08:37.183
she didn't like that back then

00:08:38.057 --> 00:08:40.278
but This Ring is the
best song I ever wrote.

00:08:40.278 --> 00:08:43.528
When I did the song I Love You she said

00:08:44.976 --> 00:08:47.333
"don't write nothing else
about if it ain't positive"

00:08:47.333 --> 00:08:50.833
and I said okay (laughs).

00:08:52.959 --> 00:08:55.034
My little girl Rainbow said
that she didn't like me

00:08:55.034 --> 00:08:57.388
to do the lewd stuff on
stage, how I would do

00:08:57.388 --> 00:09:00.987
Seven Words and lay in between the ladies.

00:09:00.987 --> 00:09:04.407
So I stopped that. I do what they say.

00:09:04.407 --> 00:09:08.313
These are the ladies that I take care of.

00:09:08.313 --> 00:09:10.564
Alyia, she's 22 now.

00:09:10.564 --> 00:09:13.648
She's out there in Oakland
having a wonderful time,

00:09:13.648 --> 00:09:15.044
doing broadcasts.

00:09:15.044 --> 00:09:17.267
She don't have too many problems.

00:09:17.267 --> 00:09:20.327
Rainbow, I can't really talk about what's

00:09:20.327 --> 00:09:22.695
going on with my little one
because she don't want it

00:09:22.695 --> 00:09:26.800
but she got sick and I just God, why me.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:29.633
She's probably like "God, why me?"

00:09:30.596 --> 00:09:35.013
my mama was sick all those
years and now my youngster.

00:09:35.013 --> 00:09:38.402
Damn, but in the midst of all that we

00:09:38.402 --> 00:09:41.566
still have time to give
ourselves to our fan

00:09:41.566 --> 00:09:43.644
and our people that want to hear it 'cause

00:09:43.644 --> 00:09:46.709
it's a blessing for people
to want to hear anything.

00:09:46.709 --> 00:09:48.518
Especially these days being in the game

00:09:48.518 --> 00:09:50.646
as long as I've been.

00:09:50.646 --> 00:09:55.180
It's such a blessing that
they still want to listen.

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:57.596
I'm going to forever have
these stories to tell

00:09:57.596 --> 00:09:59.997
because I'm writing my life
and that's what I chose

00:09:59.997 --> 00:10:02.012
to do back in the day
when Quincy Jones told me

00:10:02.012 --> 00:10:03.705
"write what you know and
people will forever feel you."

00:10:03.705 --> 00:10:05.205
- Damn, Tech N9ne.

